{
  title = "a caller's check laid on a verify copy survives the door";
  adr = "0025 item 1, 0039, jyisy";
  what = "`caller-check-residue-re-doored`: `defineType` and `mkOptionType` over `addCheck (mkOptionType (addCheck int below10) // { verify = vacuous; }) notFive`, declared twice, and `defineType` over `nullOr bolt // { verify = vacuous; }` with a check refusing `{ warp = 3; }` laid by `// { check }`, declared once, each mounted in nixpkgs' `lib.evalModules`, refuse `5`, `20` and `{ warp = 3; }` and serve `3` and `{ warp = 1; }`; gen-merge served the values the laid check rejects, because the doors answered a `verify` copy before the arm that closes a caller's check: the copy they re-completed was completed from gen data closed over the earlier check only, and the copy they returned as itself kept its completion's module-set rebuild. And `mkOptionType` over `addCheck (nullOr bolt) notTwoWarp // { verify }`, a `verify` refusing `{ warp = 2; }` laid after the check, refuses a module-function definition of `{ warp = 2; }` and serves one of `{ warp = 1; }`: the closure that keeps a laid check replaces the module-set rebuild that carried the `verify`, so it carries the `verify` again";
}
